+# Independent MesenCE capture
+
+`mesen_shot` runs a supplied NES ROM headlessly on a separate MesenCE core.
+It writes PNGs and raw nine-bit PPU indices at requested frames. `--input`
+accepts the cycle host's button schedule. Optional `--memory` also captures
+internal RAM, primary/secondary OAM and palette memory at PpuFrameDone.
+These are observation hooks, not changes to the reference emulator's algorithms.
+
+`--region ntsc|pal` selects hardware timing explicitly; the default remains
+NTSC. RAM is zeroed, sprite limit is on, and run-ahead/overclocking are off.
+The configured palette is for visual inspection; compare `.idx` files to
+avoid treating RGB palette differences as emulation differences.
+
+On macOS, supply a MesenCE libretro checkout:
+
+```sh
+bash tools/cyc/mesen_shot/build.sh /path/to/MesenCE /path/to/output
+/path/to/output/mesen_shot /private/game.nes /private/captures \
+  --region pal --input /private/route.txt --frame-offset 1 900 1200
+```
+
+The Mac build was tested against [libretro/MesenCE](https://github.com/libretro/MesenCE)
+revision `562ee84de49acbd7866d0c079e61f0dc52cc27f4`, using Apple Clang and
+the native libretro makefile. It builds no .NET UI, installs no system packages,
+and records an explicit library run path. `build.ps1` retains the existing
+Windows static-library workflow. External source/binaries/captures must remain
+outside tracked contribution files; remove their chosen directories to uninstall.
+
+Establish boot/input alignment before comparing gameplay. A one-frame boot
+offset can change sprite ordering while producing mostly identical pictures.
+Use pre-input RAM/state anchors, then apply one fixed offset to both input and
+frame numbers; do not fit an offset independently for each mismatching frame.
+This helper does not make a finite route a full-game or hardware qualification.
